WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.935
I think why I love sports
is, like--

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.971
I did a whole thing on it,
this show, once.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.906
It's the last institution
I can trust.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.441
-Mm-hmm.
-Like I don't trust anything.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.710
I don't trust the media,
I don't trust the government.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.777
STEPHEN SMITH:
I don't blame you.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.279
-No-- Right.
-I don't blame you.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.348
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS, APPLAUDS)
-I don't blame you.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.682
But I-- But--

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.418
(APPLAUSE)

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.087
There are nepo babies
everywhere.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:23.956
-Even modeling now.
-STEPHEN: Yeah.

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:26.292
You used to have to really be,
you know--

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.262
It's all the children of,
or a lot of it.

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:30.029
Okay.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.297
Politics, show business...

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.132
There are no nepo babies
in sports.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.802
Bronny James, everybody wants
to see him play with his father,

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:40.539
but he will not get on that team
unless he absolutely earns it.

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:42.708
I have total trust
that the 600 people

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:45.912
who play in baseball,
or whatever it is, 400, 500,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.481
-are the best in the world.
-STEPHEN: Right.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.817
-Am I right? Right.
-You're right about it

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:51.984
if you're talking about
the athletes.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:54.287
There's certainly nepo babies
in the front office,

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:55.788
there's nepo babies
in the coaching staff.

00:00:55.921 --> 00:00:58.258
-Right. Everywhere else.
-STEPHEN: Make no mistake
about that...

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.859
in the world of sports.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.794
But not when it comes
to the athletes.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.362
Here's the reason why.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:06.165
You're performing
in a public platform.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.267
You don't get to suck
and the audience

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.435
is going to ignore you.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.703
You're not getting away
with that.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.971
-Well, and they want to win.
-And they want--

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.239
Well, again, they want to win--

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.641
But for example,
one of the rare cases
where that happens,

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:18.877
Giannis Antetokounmpo
for the Milwaukee Bucks,

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:21.447
his little brother
is on the roster

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:24.116
and gets no playing time
whatsoever.

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:26.853
That's the closest thing
you can point to to a nepo--

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.054 line:0%
But that's about it.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.422 line:0%
You've got to be able to play.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.791 line:0%
And like with Bronny James,
here's the interesting part
about that,

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.060 line:0%
I think that kid can play,
I think he's got potential.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.194 line:0%
Is he there yet? No.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.863 line:0%
But I think he's got
the potential to be there.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.998 line:0%
But LeBron James
went front and center

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:40.166 line:0%
from day one and said,

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.568 line:0%
"I want to play in the NBA
with my son."

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.570
And because LeBron James
is still elite,

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:47.040
averaging nearly 25 a game
at the age of 39

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:50.143
in his 21st season
in professional basketball,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.112
he's such a money maker
that the thought

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:55.247
of LeBron James coming
to any franchise,

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:56.749
even if it's just for a year,

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:59.786
you're thinking about
the financial windfall
from all of that.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.121
And if LeBron comes there
and all we gotta do

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:03.356
is get Bronny James,

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.891
you never know who might
decide to do that.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.893
But in the end,
if Bronny James

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:11.130
makes it to the NBA
and he ultimately survives
in the NBA,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.965
it will be because
he can play.

00:02:13.065 --> 00:02:14.300
Not because of his dad.

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:15.534
So you're absolutely right.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.303
The nepo babies that
you're talking about,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.004
that doesn't happen
in professional sports.

00:02:19.104 --> 00:02:20.540
The public won't let you
get away with it.

